* ======================================================================
* SECTION 3: VALUE LABELS FOR RESPONSE SCALES
* ======================================================================

VALUE LABELS
  SWAI_1 SWAI_2 SWAI_3 SWAI_4 SWAI_5 SWAI_6 SWAI_7 SWAI_8 SWAI_9 SWAI_10 SWAI_11 SWAI_12 Q10 Q11 Q12 Q13 Q14 WAI_1 WAI_2 WAI_3 WAI_4 WAI_5 WAI_6 WAI_7 WAI_8 WAI_9 WAI_10 WAI_11 WAI_12 MSPSS_1 MSPSS_2 MSPSS_3 MSPSS_4 Q1 Q2 Q3 Q4 Q5 Q6 Q7 Q8 Q9
  1 'Strongly Disagree'
  2 'Disagree'
  3 'Somewhat Disagree'
  4 'Neutral'
  5 'Somewhat Agree'
  6 'Agree'
  7 'Strongly Agree'
  .
EXECUTE.

VALUE LABELS quality_flag
  'OK' 'Passed all quality checks'
  'FLAGGED' 'Quality issues detected'
  .
EXECUTE.

* ======================================================================
* SECTION 4: MISSING VALUE DECLARATIONS
* ======================================================================

* Declare system missing for out-of-range values
IF (SWAI_1 < 1 OR SWAI_1 > 7) SWAI_1 = $SYSMIS.
IF (SWAI_2 < 1 OR SWAI_2 > 7) SWAI_2 = $SYSMIS.
IF (SWAI_3 < 1 OR SWAI_3 > 7) SWAI_3 = $SYSMIS.
